.TH PROFILES 1 2000-1月 "no_catagory_profile" "no_catagory_profile"
.SH NAME
no_catagory_profile \- Create a catalog profiles object that does not contains the category information,
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIno_catagory_profile(\fBenrichments\fR as <generic> Array, 
\fBname\fR as string, 
\fBtop\fR as integer = 30, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Create a catalog profiles object that does not contains the category information,
 that means all of the enrichment terms are placed into a single catalog.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBenrichments\fB \fR\- 
 the enrichment analysis result set, both of the [EnrichmentTerm](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.Microarray.KOBAS.EnrichmentTerm) and the
 [EnrichmentResult](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSEA.EnrichmentResult) array are accepted.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBname\fB \fR\- the catalog name that will be used for the result object.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBtop\fB \fR\- the number of the most significant terms that will be kept. Default \fB30\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a [CatalogProfiles](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.ComponentModel.Annotation.CatalogProfiles) object that contains only one catalog which is named by
 the **name** parameter, or an error message when the input data type is
 not supported.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
profiles
.SH FILES
.PP
gseakit.dll
.PP
